== Description == <!--T:3-->

<!--T:4-->
The '''TechDraw StackTop''' tool moves Views to the top of the stacking order. The stacking order controls the apparent depth of Views on a page.

== Usage == <!--T:5-->

<!--T:6-->
# Select one or more Views on a [[TechDraw_PageDefault|Page]] or in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]]. For this tool, and [[TechDraw_StackBottom|TechDraw StackBottom]], the selection order is relevant.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:TechDraw_StackTop.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_StackTop|Stack Top]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|TechDraw → Stacking → [[Image:TechDraw_StackTop.svg|16px]] Stack Top}} option from the menu.
# The {{PropertyView|Stack Order}} property of the Views is changed.

==Notes==

TechDraw features having a {{PropertyView|StackOrder}} property are the [[TechDraw_View#Properties_Part_View|Part View]], formally a TechDraw::DrawViewPart object, and those derived from it:
* [[Image:TechDraw_ProjectionGroup.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_ProjectionGroup|Projection Group]]
** [[TechDraw_View#Properties_Projection_Group_Item|Projection Group Item]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_SpreadsheetView.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_SpreadsheetView|Spreadsheet View]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_ActiveView.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_ActiveView|Active View]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_ArchView.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_ArchView|BIM View]] (formerly known as an Arch View)
* [[Image:TechDraw_DraftView.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_DraftView|Draft View]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_ClipGroup.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_ClipGroup|Clip Group]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_Symbol.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_Symbol|Symbol]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_Image.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_Image|Image View]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_BrokenView.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_BrokenView|Broken View]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_SectionView.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_SectionView|Section View]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_ComplexSection.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_ComplexSection|Complex Section View]]
* [[Image:TechDraw_DetailView.svg|16px]] [[TechDraw_DetailView|Detail View]]

== Scripting == <!--T:7-->

<!--T:8-->
See also: [https://freecad.github.io/SourceDoc/ Autogenerated API documentation] and [[FreeCAD_Scripting_Basics|FreeCAD Scripting Basics]].

<!--T:9-->
The stacking order can be changed in scripts by changing the {{Incode|StackOrder}} property of a View's {{Incode|ViewObject}}.


